E_ALREADY_EXISTS	AlreadyExists	A resource with the same unique key already exists.	Choose a different name, or fetch the existing resource instead of creating a new one.	internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/mapping.go mapStateError (state.ErrAlreadyExists; producer restored in the 2026-10-01 batch-0 review after the REST 409 regression)
E_APP_HOOK_OWNED	FailedPrecondition	The app is deployed from a git hook, so material sources (image, compose, upload) are hook-owned and the deploy is refused.	Runtime changes go through spec_file (runtime overlay), env through app variables, and material through the repo. To take material ownership back, delete the hook (fleetly hooks set/get show the app's hook) or pass override_hook for a one-shot full takeover (ADR-0072).	internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/delivery.go Deploy (ADR-0072 decision 4: spec ownership split, hook-owned material gate)
E_BROWSER_UNSUPPORTED	Unimplemented	The database engine has no browse browser mapped in the dbbrowser registry.	The engine-to-browser mapping (postgres/pgvector→pgweb, redis→redis-commander, mysql→adminer, mongo→mongoku) is total over the dbtemplate value set; reaching this code means a new engine was added without a browser adapter. Extend the dbbrowser registry (ADR-0051 decision 3).	internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/databases.go BrowseDatabase — dbbrowser.go For (ADR-0051 decision 3: registry totality is the acceptance contract; unmapped engine = honest failure)
E_BROWSE_DISABLED	FailedPrecondition	The database browse face is not configured on this platform (browse.host_suffix empty).	Browse sessions need a host suffix to mint session routes. Set browse.host_suffix (and browse.gateway_url) in the fleetlyd config, then restart; absence is an explicit off state, not a degraded mode (ADR-0051 decision 5).	internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/databases.go BrowseDatabase (ADR-0051 decision 5: empty host_suffix = face disabled, precise rejection)
E_CATALOG_UNAVAILABLE	Unavailable	The template catalog refresh failed (fetch, digest verification or pre-validation).	The served catalog is unchanged. Check the configured server.templates_catalog_url, that the endpoint serves catalog.json (manifest version 1 with per-template sha256 digests), and that every entry passes validation; the error text names the failing step.	internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/templates.go RefreshTemplates (ADR-0050 decision 4: fail-closed refresh — a bad catalog never replaces a working one)
E_CHANGE_FROZEN	FailedPrecondition	A change freeze is active for the team owning this resource; the change verb is refused with the freeze reason.	Read-only and stop verbs stay available during the freeze. An operator lifts it with 'fleetly freeze lift <id>' (the freeze_id context names the row).	internal/application/governance/freeze.go (ADR-0017 appendix A.3: team-scoped change freeze, tsuru Block semantics)
E_CONFLICT	FailedPrecondition	The operation conflicts with the resource's current state.	Resolve the conflicting state named in the cause (cancel or wait for active work, remove referencing resources, or refresh after a concurrent change) and retry.	internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/mapping.go mapStateError (state.ErrConflict: CAS mismatch / FK RESTRICT); internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/structure.go DeleteApp/DeleteProject (ADR-0023); internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/platform.go TriggerPlatformBackup (备份在途 409, S3 H6); REST maps 409 via assembly errcodeToHTTP
E_DATABASE_NOT_READY	FailedPrecondition	The database is not running, so a browse session would serve a connection error page.	Wait for the database to converge to running (`fleetly databases get` shows status); browse is refused for pending/stopped databases rather than serving an unusable browser.	internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/databases.go BrowseDatabase (ADR-0051 decision 1: acceptance requires a running target — honest refusal over a broken session)
E_DATABASE_ROTATE_FAILED	FailedPrecondition	The database rejected the credential change, so the rotation did not land.	Read the error tail for the engine's own reply (auth failure or mid-flight stop are the common causes); the old credential stays valid and the rotation is retry-safe once the database is running again.	internal/application/engine/rotate.go runRotateUtility (IA v3 二期⑤b: utility-first ordering — a failed data-plane change leaves zero state behind; the secret rewrite only follows success)
E_EVENTS_GONE	FailedPrecondition	The requested event cursor is older than the earliest retained event (the retention window trimmed it).	Resynchronize: re-read the current state of the resources you track (list endpoints), then continue from the last_seq reported by GetEventStatus.	internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/contexts.go EventsService (ADR-0026: retention window + 410 + snapshot resync)
E_EXEC_UNSUPPORTED	Unimplemented	The runtime provider does not implement the exec sub-face.	Exec sessions require a runtime with RuntimeExec implemented; this deployment's runtime cannot serve them. Diagnose via `fleetly nodes list` (relay_online shows per-node relay reachability where the sub-face exists).	internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/exec.go CreateExecSession (ADR-0049 decision 1: honest failure when the sub-face is absent, no degraded path)
E_FORBIDDEN	PermissionDenied	The token lacks the scope required by this method.	Use a token whose role grants the required resource:action scope, or ask an admin for one.	internal/application/authn/interceptor.go guard (scopeSet.Satisfies)
E_GITHUB_UPSTREAM	Unavailable	The GitHub API call behind this operation failed (token minting, installation lookup, or repo listing).	Check network reachability of the configured api_base and the GitHub App installation state (suspended or uninstalled rows fail precise). Deployments retry on the next trigger once GitHub is reachable (ADR-0073).	internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/githubapps.go + internal/application/engine/gitmaterial.go resolveGitMaterial (ADR-0073 decision 3/4: verify-at-intake and build-time token minting)
E_IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_CONFLICT	AlreadyExists	The Idempotency-Key is already used by a different or in-progress request, or conflicts with the request's own idempotency_key field.	Use a fresh key for each new request. A completed response replays for 24h under the same key and the same request body; an in-progress request returns this conflict until it completes.	internal/application/idem/enforcer.go (ADR-0024: header form, single table, interceptor enforcement)
E_INTERNAL	Internal	Internal server error.	Check fleetlyd logs for the matching error_id. If the error persists, report it with the error_id attached.	internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/mapping.go mapStateError (fallback)
E_INVALID_ARGUMENT	InvalidArgument	The request payload is invalid.	Fix the flagged field and retry. Field paths point at the exact input location.	internal/domain/shared/spec/spec.go ValidationError → internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/mapping.go mapValidationError
E_INVALID_INVITATION	PermissionDenied	The invitation token is invalid, already used, or expired.	Ask an admin for a fresh invitation; invitation tokens are single-use and time-boxed.	internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/invitations.go AcceptInvitation
E_INVALID_SIGNATURE	Unauthenticated	The webhook signature verification failed.	Ensure the GitHub webhook secret matches the hook secret shown once by 'fleetly hooks set/rotate' (rotate the hook and update GitHub if the secret is lost).	internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/webhook.go ReceiveWebhook
E_LOG_STORE_UNAVAILABLE	Unavailable	The managed log store is not configured (logging.addr empty), so the persisted log-search path is unavailable.	Set logging.addr in the fleetlyd config and restart to enable log search. Live streaming without a text filter keeps working through the runtime logs sub-face (ADR-0040 dual path); absence is an explicit off state, not a degraded mode (E_REGISTRY_UNAVAILABLE precedent).	internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/contexts.go LogsService streamLogsDualPath retrieval path (P4-3 batch 3: unconfigured store = precise 503, not a masked E_INTERNAL 500)
E_MASTER_KEY_UNAVAILABLE	Unavailable	The platform has no master key configured, so the cipher face is absent and secret-backed operations are refused.	Provision the master key under the data root keys/ directory and restart fleetlyd. Absence is an explicit off state, not a degraded mode (E_REGISTRY_UNAVAILABLE precedent); sealed rows stay untouched, and there is nothing to retry until the key is in place.	internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/structure.go PutSecret — cipher-nil points also at internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/databases.go CreateDatabase, internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/templates.go InstantiateTemplate, internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/githubapps.go ListGitHubAppRepos/CompleteManifestFlow, internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/alerting.go CreateNotificationChannel (P4-3 batch 3: split from E_SECRET_UNAVAILABLE's dual semantics; the cipher face absent is an off state, not an internal fault)
E_METRICS_QUERY_TIMEOUT	DeadlineExceeded	The metrics store did not answer within the server-side query timeout.	Narrow the query or the time range and retry; the server-side timeout is 30 seconds. A client-side cancellation is not reported as this error. If it persists, check the managed metrics store health.	internal/infrastructure/providers/victoriametrics/provider.go queryRange (H8 design docs/design/2026-10-19-security-backlog-design.md §5.3.3: 30s typed timeout; parent-context cancellation excluded)
E_METRICS_RESULT_TOO_LARGE	ResourceExhausted	The metrics query result exceeds the server-side cap (response body or series count).	Narrow the PromQL query or the time range and retry. The caps are 8 MiB of response body (raw and scoped) and 1000 series (raw diagnostics); scoped queries return at most 50 series and mark the page truncated instead of failing.	internal/infrastructure/providers/victoriametrics/provider.go queryRange (H8 design docs/design/2026-10-19-security-backlog-design.md §5.3.3: body/series caps shared by raw and scoped queries)
E_METRICS_STORE_UNAVAILABLE	Unavailable	The managed metrics store is not configured (metrics.addr empty), so PromQL queries are unavailable.	Set metrics.addr in the fleetlyd config and restart to enable metrics queries; alert evaluation against the store stays off with it (ADR-0041). Absence is an explicit off state, not a degraded mode (E_REGISTRY_UNAVAILABLE precedent).	internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/alerting.go MetricsService QueryMetrics (P4-3 batch 3: unconfigured store = precise 503, not a masked E_INTERNAL 500)
E_NODE_RELAY_OFFLINE	FailedPrecondition	The target node has no connected relay, so the exec session cannot be routed to it.	Run the relay command printed by `fleetly nodes enroll` on the affected node (idempotent; it also refreshes an outdated relay after a platform upgrade), then retry. `fleetly nodes list` shows relay_online per node.	internal/application/engine/exec.go CreateSession (ADR-0049 decision 2: reverse-relay routing requires a live relay; nodes with zero inbound ports are reached only through their outbound relay)
E_NOT_CANCELLABLE	FailedPrecondition	The deployment has reached a terminal state and can no longer be cancelled.	Terminal states are facts, not actions; deploy a new revision instead.	internal/application/engine/admission.go Cancel
E_NOT_FOUND	NotFound	The requested resource does not exist.	Check the resource id and list existing resources to confirm the target.	internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/mapping.go mapStateError
E_NO_BASELINE	FailedPrecondition	The app has no successful deployment to roll back to.	Deploy at least one revision successfully before rolling back.	internal/application/engine/rollback.go Rollback
E_PLATFORM_BACKUP_FAILED	FailedPrecondition	The platform backup chain failed or is unavailable (restic missing, platform backup not configured, or the restic run failed).	Install the pinned restic version and retry; a failed platform backup is a hard stop for the upgrade sequence (ADR-0015: backup precedes the swap). The platform.backup_failed event carries the chain detail.	internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/platform.go TriggerPlatformBackup/ListPlatformBackups (ADR-0039 decision 10; F2.3 upgrade precondition)
E_QUEUE_FULL	ResourceExhausted	The deployment admission queue is full for this app.	Retry after in-flight deployments finish, or cancel a queued deployment to free a slot.	internal/application/engine/admission.go Submit (ADR-0016)
E_QUOTA_EXCEEDED	ResourceExhausted	A project-level quota has been reached.	Remove unused entries of the quoted resource, or split the workload across projects.	internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/acceptance.go taskQuota/appQuota/configQuota; internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/structure.go PutConfig (F0.17)
E_RATE_LIMITED	ResourceExhausted	The token has exhausted its create-request budget for the current rate window.	Retry after retry_after_seconds (REST also carries Retry-After). Idempotent replays do not consume budget: reuse the same Idempotency-Key to safely re-fetch a completed response.	internal/application/governance/ratelimit.go (ADR-0017 appendix A.2: per-token fixed window, in-memory, single-process control plane)
E_REGISTRY_UNAVAILABLE	Unavailable	The managed registry read proxy is unavailable (registry not configured, or the provider has no content face).	Set registry.addr in the fleetlyd config and restart to enable the managed registry; if it is already set, the configured registry provider does not serve the catalog/tags content face. Absence is an explicit off state, not a degraded mode (E_BROWSE_DISABLED precedent).	internal/application/engine/registrycontent.go registryContentFor (IA v3 二期⑤b/P0-7: unconfigured face = precise 503, not a masked 500)
E_RUNTIME_FACE_UNSUPPORTED	Unimplemented	The runtime provider does not expose the optional sub-face this operation needs (node administration, container logs or node relay material), or the engine face is absent.	The sub-face set is provider-dependent: node drain/cordon/uncordon and live container logs need a runtime with RuntimeAdmin/RuntimeLogs implemented, node relay material needs RuntimeRelayMaterial, and carrier restart additionally needs the engine face. There is no degraded path (E_EXEC_UNSUPPORTED precedent); serve the operation from a runtime that implements the face.	internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/contexts.go NodesService nodeAdmin/enrollRelayMaterial + LogsService streamLogsDualPath; internal/interfaces/grpc/systemgrpc/systemgrpc.go RestartComponent (P4-3 batch 3: absent optional face = precise 501, not a masked E_INTERNAL 500; E_EXEC_UNSUPPORTED/E_BROWSER_UNSUPPORTED precedent)
E_SECRET_UNAVAILABLE	FailedPrecondition	A secret seal or open operation failed while the master key is configured (cipher operation error).	The message names the failing operation and carries the cipher error text. Check that the master key under the data root keys/ directory is the same one that sealed the payload — a replaced or rotated key cannot open old envelopes.	internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/webhook.go ReceiveWebhook (open), internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/hooks.go SetGitHook/RotateHookToken (seal), internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/githubapps.go private-key seal/open paths (P4-3 batch 3: narrowed to cipher-operation failures — the no-master-key nil face moved to E_MASTER_KEY_UNAVAILABLE)
E_TEMPLATE_INVALID	InvalidArgument	An app template document failed to parse, render or validate.	The error names the template field at fault. If the template came from a catalog refresh, the refresh pre-validation should have caught it; report the template name@version (in the message) with the error text.	internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/templates.go InstantiateTemplate (ADR-0050 decision 2: fail-closed render chain; refresh pre-validates the same entry points, so reaching this code means a template defect)
E_UNAUTHENTICATED	Unauthenticated	The request carries no valid token.	Log in with a valid token ('fleetly login'), or check that the token has not been revoked.	internal/application/authn/interceptor.go guard
E_UPLOAD_TOO_LARGE	ResourceExhausted	The uploaded source exceeds the per-upload size limit.	Exclude build-irrelevant files from the directory (e.g. .git), or build from a git reference instead.	internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/uploads.go UploadSource (ADR-0019 appendix A.3: streaming byte budget, 512MiB default)
E_UPLOAD_UNAVAILABLE	FailedPrecondition	The uploaded source referenced by this deploy no longer has its blob on disk.	The upload was likely affected by a retention sweep or a data-root migration; upload the source again and redeploy.	internal/interfaces/grpc/fleetlygrpc/delivery.go Deploy (ADR-0019 appendix A.5)
